<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Flour says buys 15,400T of U.S. No.1 wheat.</title>
<headline>Korea Flour says buys 15,400T of U.S. No.1 wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Flour Milling Corp said it bought 15,400 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat on Tuesday from Japanese trading house Kanematsu Corp.</p>
<p>A company official said arrival was set to the southwestern port of Mokpo.</p>
<p>Shipment was slated for March 10-April 10 from the Pacific Northwest, the official said.  </p>
<p>Details of the purchase are as follows:</p>
<p>  TYPE OF WHEAT	     TONNE	PRICE/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  6,000	 $149.55</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  3,500	 $147.75</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	   2,300	 $176.75</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    3,600	 $177.75</p>
<p>(and/or Northern Spring)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
